                            <a name="comment194"></a>
<h4 class="boldbyline">
Re: Waiting On Wilma
</h4>

<p>
LINCOLN, Neb. -- Even as record-setting Hurricane Wilma plodded toward the west coast of Florida and sent tourist fleeing the Keys, last month's devastating Hurricane Katrina, which ravaged New Orleans and other Gulf Coast cities, was holed up in a Days Inn outside Lincoln, keeping authorities at bay with threatening rain bands, police said.<br />
"The good thing is, we know where she is," said Lincoln police spokeswoman Michelle Miller. "The bad thing is, this storm is still a Category 1, and we found empty bottles of Jack Daniels in the hallway trashcan."<br />
Authorities have been searching for Katrina since early September, when she crashed into coastal cities in Mississippi, Louisiana and Alabama, killing many, greatly embarrassing unprepared FEMA chief Michael Brown and helping to reveal that President Bush really doesn't like black people.
</p>
